<Base title="About — EllixTech"><section class="wrap page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">A LITTLE CURIOSITY. A LOT OF BUILDING.</div><h1>Technology,<br/>with intention<span class="coral-period">.</span></h1><p>EllixTech is an independent journal about the craft of building software.</p></section><section class="wrap about-body prose"><h2>Understand the why.</h2><p>The most useful technical writing does more than share a solution. It makes the tradeoffs visible, explains the mental model, and gives you something worth trying.</p><p>Here, we explore web engineering, developer tools, and the systems underneath them. Expect practical tutorials, considered perspectives, and room for curiosity.</p><h2>Built in the open.</h2><p>This publication is built with Astro, TypeScript, and MDX. Its source is available on GitHub, because the way we build should be as open as the ideas we share.</p><a class="button" href="https://github.com/EllixTech/ellixtech">Explore the source ↗</a><h2>Two languages. One curious mindset.</h2><p>EllixTech supports English and Spanish content. Each article declares its language, so writers can publish in either language without changing the site's architecture.</p></section></Base>
